<h1>VoiceTel Phone for macOS.</h1>
<p class="lede">Download, install, and troubleshoot the macOS app (.dmg or .zip) on Apple Silicon and Intel Macs. VoiceML Phone, the same softphone for VoiceML accounts, is listed alongside.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Sign up</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/phone/applications/desktop/">All desktop clients</a>
</p>

<section id="download" class="section-block">
	<h2>1. Download</h2>
	<p>Choose the build that matches your Mac: <strong>arm64</strong> for Apple Silicon (M1&ndash;M4), <strong>x86-64</strong> for Intel. If unsure, use the <strong>.dmg</strong>. All macOS builds are signed and notarized by Apple, so Gatekeeper opens them without warnings.</p>
	{% include "partials/phone-desktop-downloads.njk" %}
</section>

<section id="verify" class="section-block">
	<h2>2. Verify checksum (optional)</h2>
	<p>Validate file integrity by comparing SHA-256 checksums.</p>
	<ol>
		<li>Open <code>Terminal</code>.</li>
		<li>Run: <code>shasum -a 256 VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}-arm64.dmg</code> (or whichever file you downloaded).</li>
		<li>Compare the output with the value listed above.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section id="install" class="section-block">
	<h2>3. Install</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Open the downloaded <strong>.dmg</strong>.</li>
		<li>Drag <strong>VoiceTel</strong> (or <strong>VoiceML</strong>) to the <strong>Applications</strong> folder. Eject the disk image when finished.</li>
		<li>For scripted installs, unzip the <strong>.zip</strong> and move <code>VoiceTel.app</code> (or <code>VoiceML.app</code>) to Applications.</li>
	</ol>
	<p><strong>Upgrading?</strong> Fully quit the running app from the menu-bar icon (right-click &rarr; <em>Quit</em>) before installing; otherwise the single-instance lock re-focuses the old version.</p>
</section>

<section id="firstlaunch" class="section-block">
	<h2>4. First launch</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Open <strong>VoiceTel</strong> from Applications.</li>
		<li>Allow microphone access when prompted. If you missed the prompt, go to <em>System Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security &rarr; Microphone</em> and enable access for the app.</li>
		<li>Enter your VoiceTel SIP credentials (username, password, display name) as provisioned in the customer portal. In VoiceML Phone, enter your VoiceML activation code under <em>Settings &rarr; Auto Provision</em> instead.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="section-block faq-block">
	<h2>FAQ</h2>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>How do I uninstall VoiceTel Phone?</summary>
		<p>Quit the app, open <em>Applications</em>, and drag <strong>VoiceTel.app</strong> (or <strong>VoiceML.app</strong>) to the Trash.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>The app won't open after installation</summary>
		<p>The builds are notarized, so Gatekeeper should open them directly. If your Mac's security policy still blocks the app, right-click it and choose <em>Open</em>, or go to <em>System Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security</em> and click <em>Open Anyway</em>.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>The microphone isn't working</summary>
		<p>Ensure the app has permission under <em>System Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security &rarr; Microphone</em>. Also check <em>System Settings &rarr; Sound</em> for the correct input device.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Can I pre-configure the app for my users?</summary>
		<p>Yes. Place <code>voicetel.json</code> under <code>~/Library/Application Support/VoiceTelPhone/</code> for user-level deployment, or <code>/Library/Application Support/VoiceTelPhone/</code> for system-wide deployment.</p>
	</details>
</section>

